  "details": "I'm pretty apprehensive to make this request because it would be a large endeavor for the develops. Me and other world authors feel very limited by unity's audio implementation. Implementation of audio in most game requires scripting to really fine tune the audio, or developers use middleware tools such as wwise. This would allow world creators to create dynamic sound scapes and music for their worlds, all without scripting. Wwise's audio compression is also top notch. Would love to see this even if I have to wait.",
